{"id": 3753, "slug": "wage-and-hour-lawyer", "content_raw": "<!-- wp:freeform --><p>Before proceeding, please review the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://langefirm.com/legal-disclaimer/\"> <b>legal disclaimer.</b></a></p>\n<h1 data-start=\"417\" data-end=\"485\"><strong data-start=\"419\" data-end=\"485\">Wage and Hour Lawyer in Texas: Fight for the Pay You\u2019ve Earned</strong></h1>\n<p data-start=\"487\" data-end=\"658\">Have you been shorted on your paycheck? Denied overtime? Paid late or off the books? These are not just workplace frustrations\u2014they\u2019re violations of state and federal law.</p>\n<p data-start=\"660\" data-end=\"775\">If you\u2019re dealing with wage theft or unfair pay practices, it may be time to speak with a <strong data-start=\"750\" data-end=\"774\">wage and hour lawyer</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"1060\">At <strong data-start=\"780\" data-end=\"798\">The Lange Firm</strong>, we represent employees across Texas who\u2019ve been underpaid, misclassified, or otherwise cheated out of what they\u2019ve rightfully earned. In this comprehensive guide, we\u2019ll explain your rights, what violations to look for, how to file a claim, and how we can help.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"2057\" data-end=\"2060\">\n<h2 data-start=\"2062\" data-end=\"2105\"><strong data-start=\"2065\" data-end=\"2105\">What Does a Wage and Hour Lawyer Do?</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"2107\" data-end=\"2253\">A <strong data-start=\"2109\" data-end=\"2133\">wage and hour lawyer</strong> helps employees recover unpaid wages, enforce labor rights, and pursue damages against employers who violate wage laws.</p>\n<p data-start=\"2255\" data-end=\"2301\">At <strong data-start=\"2258\" data-end=\"2276\">The Lange Firm</strong>, we assist clients with:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"2303\" data-end=\"2529\">\n<li data-start=\"2303\" data-end=\"2322\">\n<p data-start=\"2305\" data-end=\"2322\">Unpaid overtime</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2323\" data-end=\"2350\">\n<p data-start=\"2325\" data-end=\"2350\">Minimum wage violations</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2351\" data-end=\"2373\">\n<p data-start=\"2353\" data-end=\"2373\">Illegal deductions</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2374\" data-end=\"2435\">\n<p data-start=\"2376\" data-end=\"2435\">Misclassification of employees as independent contractors</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2436\" data-end=\"2466\">\n<p data-start=\"2438\" data-end=\"2466\">Denied meal or rest breaks</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2467\" data-end=\"2480\">\n<p data-start=\"2469\" data-end=\"2480\">Tip theft</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2481\" data-end=\"2508\">\n<p data-start=\"2483\" data-end=\"2508\">Final paycheck disputes</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2509\" data-end=\"2529\">\n<p data-start=\"2511\" data-end=\"2529\">Off-the-clock work</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"2531\" data-end=\"2645\">Whether you\u2019ve lost hundreds or thousands in unpaid wages, you may be entitled to <strong data-start=\"2613\" data-end=\"2644\">compensation plus penalties</strong>.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"2647\" data-end=\"2650\">\n<h2 data-start=\"2652\" data-end=\"2690\"><strong data-start=\"2655\" data-end=\"2690\">Common Wage and Hour Violations</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"2692\" data-end=\"2745\">Here are some of the most frequent violations we see:</p>\n<h3 data-start=\"2747\" data-end=\"2775\">\u2705 1. <strong data-start=\"2756\" data-end=\"2775\">Unpaid Overtime</strong></h3>\n<p data-start=\"2776\" data-end=\"2894\">You\u2019re entitled to <strong data-start=\"2795\" data-end=\"2828\">1.5x your regular hourly rate</strong> for hours worked beyond 40 per week\u2014unless you\u2019re legally exempt.</p>\n<h3 data-start=\"2896\" data-end=\"2936\">\u2705 2. <strong data-start=\"2905\" data-end=\"2936\">Misclassification as Exempt</strong></h3>\n<p data-start=\"2937\" data-end=\"3032\">Many employers <strong data-start=\"2952\" data-end=\"2972\">mislabel workers</strong> as \u201cexempt\u201d from overtime when they legally qualify for it.</p>\n<h3 data-start=\"3034\" data-end=\"3070\">\u2705 3. <strong data-start=\"3043\" data-end=\"3070\">Minimum Wage Violations</strong></h3>\n<p data-start=\"3071\" data-end=\"3189\">Texas follows the federal minimum wage of <strong data-start=\"3113\" data-end=\"3127\">$7.25/hour</strong>. Tipped workers must still earn at least that <strong data-start=\"3174\" data-end=\"3188\">after tips</strong>.</p>\n<h3 data-start=\"3191\" data-end=\"3222\">\u2705 4. <strong data-start=\"3200\" data-end=\"3222\">Off-the-Clock Work</strong></h3>\n<p data-start=\"3223\" data-end=\"3343\">If you're forced to work before clocking in, during unpaid breaks, or after your shift, that\u2019s <strong data-start=\"3318\" data-end=\"3342\">illegal unpaid labor</strong>.</p>\n<h3 data-start=\"3345\" data-end=\"3376\">\u2705 5. <strong data-start=\"3354\" data-end=\"3376\">Illegal Deductions</strong></h3>\n<p data-start=\"3377\" data-end=\"3519\">Employers can\u2019t deduct wages for uniforms, damages, or shortages without written consent\u2014and can never reduce your pay <strong data-start=\"3496\" data-end=\"3518\">below minimum wage</strong>.</p>\n<h3 data-start=\"3521\" data-end=\"3559\">\u2705 6. <strong data-start=\"3530\" data-end=\"3559\">Not Paying Final Paycheck</strong></h3>\n<p data-start=\"3560\" data-end=\"3655\">Texas law requires final wages to be paid within <strong data-start=\"3609\" data-end=\"3619\">6 days</strong> of termination for fired employees.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"3657\" data-end=\"3660\">\n<h2 data-start=\"3662\" data-end=\"3724\"><strong data-start=\"3665\" data-end=\"3724\">What Are Your Legal Rights Under Texas and Federal Law?</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"3726\" data-end=\"3755\">Your rights are protected by:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"3757\" data-end=\"4007\">\n<li data-start=\"3757\" data-end=\"3814\">\n<p data-start=\"3759\" data-end=\"3814\"><strong data-start=\"3759\" data-end=\"3798\">The Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA)</strong> \u2013 Federal law</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3815\" data-end=\"3874\">\n<p data-start=\"3817\" data-end=\"3874\"><strong data-start=\"3817\" data-end=\"3837\">Texas Payday Law</strong> \u2013 State law on timely wage payment</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3875\" data-end=\"3937\">\n<p data-start=\"3877\" data-end=\"3937\"><strong data-start=\"3877\" data-end=\"3906\">Department of Labor (DOL)</strong> \u2013 Federal enforcement agency</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3938\" data-end=\"4007\">\n<p data-start=\"3940\" data-end=\"4007\"><strong data-start=\"3940\" data-end=\"3976\">Texas Workforce Commission (TWC)</strong> \u2013 State agency for wage claims</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"4009\" data-end=\"4050\">Employers who violate these laws may owe:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"4052\" data-end=\"4168\">\n<li data-start=\"4052\" data-end=\"4068\">\n<p data-start=\"4054\" data-end=\"4068\"><strong data-start=\"4054\" data-end=\"4066\">Back pay</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4069\" data-end=\"4120\">\n<p data-start=\"4071\" data-end=\"4120\"><strong data-start=\"4071\" data-end=\"4093\">Liquidated damages</strong> (double the amount owed)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4121\" data-end=\"4139\">\n<p data-start=\"4123\" data-end=\"4139\"><strong data-start=\"4123\" data-end=\"4137\">Legal fees</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4140\" data-end=\"4168\">\n<p data-start=\"4142\" data-end=\"4168\"><strong data-start=\"4142\" data-end=\"4168\">Interest and penalties</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start=\"4170\" data-end=\"4173\">\n<h2 data-start=\"4175\" data-end=\"4224\"><strong data-start=\"4178\" data-end=\"4224\">Who Is Protected Under Wage and Hour Laws?</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"4226\" data-end=\"4270\">Nearly all employees are covered, including:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"4272\" data-end=\"4428\">\n<li data-start=\"4272\" data-end=\"4290\">\n<p data-start=\"4274\" data-end=\"4290\">Hourly workers</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4291\" data-end=\"4324\">\n<p data-start=\"4293\" data-end=\"4324\">Salaried non-exempt employees</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4325\" data-end=\"4345\">\n<p data-start=\"4327\" data-end=\"4345\">Tipped employees</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4346\" data-end=\"4373\">\n<p data-start=\"4348\" data-end=\"4373\">Interns (in some cases)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4374\" data-end=\"4428\">\n<p data-start=\"4376\" data-end=\"4428\">Freelancers misclassified as independent contractors</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"4430\" data-end=\"4555\">However, some <strong data-start=\"4444\" data-end=\"4464\">exempt employees</strong>\u2014like executives, professionals, and some outside salespeople\u2014may not qualify for overtime.</p>\n<p data-start=\"4557\" data-end=\"4683\">A <strong data-start=\"4559\" data-end=\"4583\">wage and hour lawyer</strong> at <strong data-start=\"4587\" data-end=\"4605\">The Lange Firm</strong> can review your job duties to determine whether you were properly classified.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"4685\" data-end=\"4688\">\n<h2 data-start=\"4690\" data-end=\"4744\"><strong data-start=\"4693\" data-end=\"4744\">Signs You Should Contact a Wage and Hour Lawyer</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"4746\" data-end=\"4776\">You should seek legal help if:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"4778\" data-end=\"5197\">\n<li data-start=\"4778\" data-end=\"4841\">\n<p data-start=\"4780\" data-end=\"4841\">You regularly work over 40 hours and don\u2019t receive overtime</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4842\" data-end=\"4885\">\n<p data-start=\"4844\" data-end=\"4885\">You\u2019re not paid minimum wage after tips</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4886\" data-end=\"4944\">\n<p data-start=\"4888\" data-end=\"4944\">Your employer asks you to \u201cclock out and keep working\u201d</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4945\" data-end=\"4994\">\n<p data-start=\"4947\" data-end=\"4994\">Your paycheck contains unexplained deductions</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"4995\" data-end=\"5041\">\n<p data-start=\"4997\" data-end=\"5041\">You haven\u2019t been paid for all hours worked</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5042\" data-end=\"5084\">\n<p data-start=\"5044\" data-end=\"5084\">You didn\u2019t receive your final paycheck</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5085\" data-end=\"5145\">\n<p data-start=\"5087\" data-end=\"5145\">You\u2019re asked to sign away your rights or confidentiality</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5146\" data-end=\"5197\">\n<p data-start=\"5148\" data-end=\"5197\">You\u2019re fired after asking about pay discrepancies</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"5199\" data-end=\"5293\">Don\u2019t wait\u2014<strong data-start=\"5210\" data-end=\"5254\">Texas wage claims have short time limits</strong>, and the clock may already be ticking.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"5295\" data-end=\"5298\">\n<h2 data-start=\"5300\" data-end=\"5345\"><strong data-start=\"5303\" data-end=\"5345\">How to Prove a Wage and Hour Violation</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"5347\" data-end=\"5371\">Evidence is key. Gather:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"5373\" data-end=\"5571\">\n<li data-start=\"5373\" data-end=\"5403\">\n<p data-start=\"5375\" data-end=\"5403\">Timecards or punch records</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5404\" data-end=\"5436\">\n<p data-start=\"5406\" data-end=\"5436\">Paystubs and wage statements</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5437\" data-end=\"5472\">\n<p data-start=\"5439\" data-end=\"5472\">Work schedules or text messages</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5473\" data-end=\"5497\">\n<p data-start=\"5475\" data-end=\"5497\">Emails from managers</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5498\" data-end=\"5535\">\n<p data-start=\"5500\" data-end=\"5535\">Screenshots from clock-in systems</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5536\" data-end=\"5571\">\n<p data-start=\"5538\" data-end=\"5571\">Witness statements from coworkers</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"5573\" data-end=\"5715\">Even if you don\u2019t have perfect records, <strong data-start=\"5613\" data-end=\"5631\">The Lange Firm</strong> can help reconstruct your case and use subpoena power to demand employer documents.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"5717\" data-end=\"5720\">\n<h2 data-start=\"5722\" data-end=\"5752\"><strong data-start=\"5725\" data-end=\"5752\">Damages You May Recover</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"5754\" data-end=\"5805\">Employees who win wage and hour claims may recover:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"5807\" data-end=\"5994\">\n<li data-start=\"5807\" data-end=\"5827\">\n<p data-start=\"5809\" data-end=\"5827\"><strong data-start=\"5809\" data-end=\"5825\">Unpaid wages</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5828\" data-end=\"5848\">\n<p data-start=\"5830\" data-end=\"5848\"><strong data-start=\"5830\" data-end=\"5846\">Overtime pay</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5849\" data-end=\"5901\">\n<p data-start=\"5851\" data-end=\"5901\"><strong data-start=\"5851\" data-end=\"5873\">Liquidated damages</strong> (up to 2x the wages owed)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5902\" data-end=\"5925\">\n<p data-start=\"5904\" data-end=\"5925\"><strong data-start=\"5904\" data-end=\"5923\">Attorney\u2019s fees</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5926\" data-end=\"5956\">\n<p data-start=\"5928\" data-end=\"5956\"><strong data-start=\"5928\" data-end=\"5954\">Interest and penalties</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"5957\" data-end=\"5994\">\n<p data-start=\"5959\" data-end=\"5994\">In rare cases, <strong data-start=\"5974\" data-end=\"5994\">punitive damages</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"5996\" data-end=\"6085\">In class or collective actions, entire groups of employees may recover large settlements.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"6087\" data-end=\"6090\">\n<h2 data-start=\"6092\" data-end=\"6142\"><strong data-start=\"6095\" data-end=\"6142\">What to Expect When You Hire The Lange Firm</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"6144\" data-end=\"6174\">Here\u2019s what we do for clients:</p>\n<ol data-start=\"6176\" data-end=\"6443\">\n<li data-start=\"6176\" data-end=\"6222\">\n<p data-start=\"6179\" data-end=\"6222\"><strong data-start=\"6179\" data-end=\"6200\">Initial consultation</strong> to assess your case</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"6223\" data-end=\"6278\">\n<p data-start=\"6226\" data-end=\"6278\"><strong data-start=\"6226\" data-end=\"6244\">Legal analysis</strong> of wage and hour law violations</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"6279\" data-end=\"6336\">\n<p data-start=\"6282\" data-end=\"6336\"><strong data-start=\"6282\" data-end=\"6308\">Settlement negotiation</strong> or employer demand letter</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"6337\" data-end=\"6379\">\n<p data-start=\"6340\" data-end=\"6379\"><strong data-start=\"6340\" data-end=\"6366\">Filing with DOL or TWC</strong>, if needed</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"6380\" data-end=\"6443\">\n<p data-start=\"6383\" data-end=\"6443\"><strong data-start=\"6383\" data-end=\"6420\">Lawsuit in state or federal court</strong>, if employer won\u2019t pay</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-start=\"6445\" data-end=\"6554\">We handle many cases on a <strong data-start=\"6471\" data-end=\"6496\">contingency fee basis</strong>\u2014meaning no legal fees unless we win or settle your claim.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"6556\" data-end=\"6559\">\n<h2 data-start=\"6561\" data-end=\"6604\"><strong data-start=\"6564\" data-end=\"6604\">Texas Wage and Hour Laws at a Glance</strong></h2>\n<table data-start=\"6606\" data-end=\"7236\">\n<thead data-start=\"6606\" data-end=\"6683\">\n<tr data-start=\"6606\" data-end=\"6683\">\n<th data-start=\"6606\" data-end=\"6636\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"6608\" data-end=\"6620\">Category</strong></th>\n<th data-start=\"6636\" data-end=\"6683\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"6638\" data-end=\"6646\">Rule</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody data-start=\"6763\" data-end=\"7236\">\n<tr data-start=\"6763\" data-end=\"6841\">\n<td data-start=\"6763\" data-end=\"6793\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Minimum Wage</td>\n<td data-start=\"6793\" data-end=\"6841\" data-col-size=\"md\">$7.25/hour (federal and Texas rate)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"6842\" data-end=\"6920\">\n<td data-start=\"6842\" data-end=\"6872\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Overtime</td>\n<td data-start=\"6872\" data-end=\"6920\" data-col-size=\"md\">Time-and-a-half for hours &gt; 40/week</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"6921\" data-end=\"6999\">\n<td data-start=\"6921\" data-end=\"6951\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Final Paycheck</td>\n<td data-start=\"6951\" data-end=\"6999\" data-col-size=\"md\">Within 6 days if fired, next payday if quit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"7000\" data-end=\"7078\">\n<td data-start=\"7000\" data-end=\"7030\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Deductions</td>\n<td data-start=\"7030\" data-end=\"7078\" data-col-size=\"md\">Must be authorized and legal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"7079\" data-end=\"7157\">\n<td data-start=\"7079\" data-end=\"7109\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Tip Credit</td>\n<td data-start=\"7109\" data-end=\"7157\" data-col-size=\"md\">Employer can claim up to $5.12/hour</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"7158\" data-end=\"7236\">\n<td data-start=\"7158\" data-end=\"7188\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Breaks</td>\n<td data-start=\"7188\" data-end=\"7236\" data-col-size=\"md\">Not legally required (except nursing moms)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n&nbsp;\n<hr data-start=\"7238\" data-end=\"7241\">\n<h2 data-start=\"7243\" data-end=\"7287\"><strong data-start=\"7246\" data-end=\"7287\">Industries Where Wage Theft Is Common</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"7289\" data-end=\"7355\">Some industries have <strong data-start=\"7310\" data-end=\"7354\">higher rates of wage and hour violations</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"7357\" data-end=\"7530\">\n<li data-start=\"7357\" data-end=\"7373\">\n<p data-start=\"7359\" data-end=\"7373\">Construction</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"7374\" data-end=\"7390\">\n<p data-start=\"7376\" data-end=\"7390\">Food service</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"7391\" data-end=\"7406\">\n<p data-start=\"7393\" data-end=\"7406\">Hospitality</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"7407\" data-end=\"7417\">\n<p data-start=\"7409\" data-end=\"7417\">Retail</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"7418\" data-end=\"7441\">\n<p data-start=\"7420\" data-end=\"7441\">Janitorial services</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"7442\" data-end=\"7482\">\n<p data-start=\"7444\" data-end=\"7482\">Healthcare (home care workers, CNAs)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"7483\" data-end=\"7515\">\n<p data-start=\"7485\" data-end=\"7515\">Transportation and logistics</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"7516\" data-end=\"7530\">\n<p data-start=\"7518\" data-end=\"7530\">Call centers</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"7532\" data-end=\"7669\">\ud83d\udccc If you work in one of these sectors, speak to <strong data-start=\"7581\" data-end=\"7599\">The Lange Firm</strong> about your pay practices\u2014especially if you\u2019ve noticed irregularities.</p>\n<hr data-start=\"7671\" data-end=\"7674\">\n<h2 data-start=\"7676\" data-end=\"7697\"><strong data-start=\"7679\" data-end=\"7697\">Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n<p data-start=\"7699\" data-end=\"7742\">So what does a <strong data-start=\"7714\" data-end=\"7738\">wage and hour lawyer</strong> do?</p>\n<p data-start=\"7744\" data-end=\"7857\">\u2705 We fight for your wages.<br data-start=\"7770\" data-end=\"7773\">\u2705 We hold employers accountable.<br data-start=\"7805\" data-end=\"7808\">\u2705 We help you get justice\u2014one paycheck at a time.</p>\n<p data-start=\"7859\" data-end=\"8018\">At <strong data-start=\"7862\" data-end=\"7880\">The Lange Firm</strong>, we\u2019ve seen how underpayment affects real lives. Don\u2019t settle for less than you\u2019ve earned. Let us help you claim what\u2019s rightfully yours.</p>\n<p data-start=\"8020\" data-end=\"8070\">\ud83d\udcde <strong data-start=\"8023\" data-end=\"8070\">Call today for a confidential consultation.</strong></p>\n<p><!-- /wp:freeform --></p><!-- /wp:post-content -->", "_elementor_data": "[{\"id\":\"427cb84c\",\"elType\":\"container\",\"settings\":[],\"elements\":[{\"id\":\"285a3b76\",\"elType\":\"widget\",\"settings\":{\"editor\":\"<p><span style=\\\"font-weight: 400;\\\">Before proceeding, please review the<\\/span>&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/langefirm.com\\/legal-disclaimer\\/\\\"> <b>legal disclaimer.<\\/b><\\/a><\\/p>\\n<h1 data-start=\\\"417\\\" data-end=\\\"485\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"419\\\" data-end=\\\"485\\\">Wage and Hour Lawyer in Texas: Fight for the Pay You\\u2019ve Earned<\\/strong><\\/h1>\\n<p data-start=\\\"487\\\" data-end=\\\"658\\\">Have you been shorted on your paycheck? Denied overtime? Paid late or off the books? These are not just workplace frustrations\\u2014they\\u2019re violations of state and federal law.<\\/p>\\n<p data-start=\\\"660\\\" data-end=\\\"775\\\">If you\\u2019re dealing with wage theft or unfair pay practices, it may be time to speak with a <strong data-start=\\\"750\\\" data-end=\\\"774\\\">wage and hour lawyer<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\n<p data-start=\\\"777\\\" data-end=\\\"1060\\\">At <strong data-start=\\\"780\\\" data-end=\\\"798\\\">The Lange Firm<\\/strong>, we represent employees across Texas who\\u2019ve been underpaid, misclassified, or otherwise cheated out of what they\\u2019ve rightfully earned. In this comprehensive guide, we\\u2019ll explain your rights, what violations to look for, how to file a claim, and how we can help.<\\/p>\\n<hr data-start=\\\"2057\\\" data-end=\\\"2060\\\">\\n<h2 data-start=\\\"2062\\\" data-end=\\\"2105\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"2065\\\" data-end=\\\"2105\\\">What Does a Wage and Hour Lawyer Do?<\\/strong><\\/h2>\\n<p data-start=\\\"2107\\\" data-end=\\\"2253\\\">A <strong data-start=\\\"2109\\\" data-end=\\\"2133\\\">wage and hour lawyer<\\/strong> helps employees recover unpaid wages, enforce labor rights, and pursue damages against employers who violate wage laws.<\\/p>\\n<p data-start=\\\"2255\\\" data-end=\\\"2301\\\">At <strong data-start=\\\"2258\\\" data-end=\\\"2276\\\">The Lange Firm<\\/strong>, we assist clients with:<\\/p>\\n<ul data-start=\\\"2303\\\" data-end=\\\"2529\\\">\\n<li data-start=\\\"2303\\\" data-end=\\\"2322\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"2305\\\" data-end=\\\"2322\\\">Unpaid overtime<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"2323\\\" data-end=\\\"2350\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"2325\\\" data-end=\\\"2350\\\">Minimum wage violations<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"2351\\\" data-end=\\\"2373\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"2353\\\" data-end=\\\"2373\\\">Illegal deductions<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"2374\\\" data-end=\\\"2435\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"2376\\\" data-end=\\\"2435\\\">Misclassification of employees as independent contractors<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"2436\\\" data-end=\\\"2466\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"2438\\\" data-end=\\\"2466\\\">Denied meal or rest breaks<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"2467\\\" data-end=\\\"2480\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"2469\\\" data-end=\\\"2480\\\">Tip theft<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"2481\\\" data-end=\\\"2508\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"2483\\\" data-end=\\\"2508\\\">Final paycheck disputes<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"2509\\\" data-end=\\\"2529\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"2511\\\" data-end=\\\"2529\\\">Off-the-clock work<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p data-start=\\\"2531\\\" data-end=\\\"2645\\\">Whether you\\u2019ve lost hundreds or thousands in unpaid wages, you may be entitled to <strong data-start=\\\"2613\\\" data-end=\\\"2644\\\">compensation plus penalties<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\n<hr data-start=\\\"2647\\\" data-end=\\\"2650\\\">\\n<h2 data-start=\\\"2652\\\" data-end=\\\"2690\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"2655\\\" data-end=\\\"2690\\\">Common Wage and Hour Violations<\\/strong><\\/h2>\\n<p data-start=\\\"2692\\\" data-end=\\\"2745\\\">Here are some of the most frequent violations we see:<\\/p>\\n<h3 data-start=\\\"2747\\\" data-end=\\\"2775\\\">\\u2705 1. <strong data-start=\\\"2756\\\" data-end=\\\"2775\\\">Unpaid Overtime<\\/strong><\\/h3>\\n<p data-start=\\\"2776\\\" data-end=\\\"2894\\\">You\\u2019re entitled to <strong data-start=\\\"2795\\\" data-end=\\\"2828\\\">1.5x your regular hourly rate<\\/strong> for hours worked beyond 40 per week\\u2014unless you\\u2019re legally exempt.<\\/p>\\n<h3 data-start=\\\"2896\\\" data-end=\\\"2936\\\">\\u2705 2. <strong data-start=\\\"2905\\\" data-end=\\\"2936\\\">Misclassification as Exempt<\\/strong><\\/h3>\\n<p data-start=\\\"2937\\\" data-end=\\\"3032\\\">Many employers <strong data-start=\\\"2952\\\" data-end=\\\"2972\\\">mislabel workers<\\/strong> as \\u201cexempt\\u201d from overtime when they legally qualify for it.<\\/p>\\n<h3 data-start=\\\"3034\\\" data-end=\\\"3070\\\">\\u2705 3. <strong data-start=\\\"3043\\\" data-end=\\\"3070\\\">Minimum Wage Violations<\\/strong><\\/h3>\\n<p data-start=\\\"3071\\\" data-end=\\\"3189\\\">Texas follows the federal minimum wage of <strong data-start=\\\"3113\\\" data-end=\\\"3127\\\">$7.25\\/hour<\\/strong>. Tipped workers must still earn at least that <strong data-start=\\\"3174\\\" data-end=\\\"3188\\\">after tips<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\n<h3 data-start=\\\"3191\\\" data-end=\\\"3222\\\">\\u2705 4. <strong data-start=\\\"3200\\\" data-end=\\\"3222\\\">Off-the-Clock Work<\\/strong><\\/h3>\\n<p data-start=\\\"3223\\\" data-end=\\\"3343\\\">If you're forced to work before clocking in, during unpaid breaks, or after your shift, that\\u2019s <strong data-start=\\\"3318\\\" data-end=\\\"3342\\\">illegal unpaid labor<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\n<h3 data-start=\\\"3345\\\" data-end=\\\"3376\\\">\\u2705 5. <strong data-start=\\\"3354\\\" data-end=\\\"3376\\\">Illegal Deductions<\\/strong><\\/h3>\\n<p data-start=\\\"3377\\\" data-end=\\\"3519\\\">Employers can\\u2019t deduct wages for uniforms, damages, or shortages without written consent\\u2014and can never reduce your pay <strong data-start=\\\"3496\\\" data-end=\\\"3518\\\">below minimum wage<\\/strong>.<\\/p>\\n<h3 data-start=\\\"3521\\\" data-end=\\\"3559\\\">\\u2705 6. <strong data-start=\\\"3530\\\" data-end=\\\"3559\\\">Not Paying Final Paycheck<\\/strong><\\/h3>\\n<p data-start=\\\"3560\\\" data-end=\\\"3655\\\">Texas law requires final wages to be paid within <strong data-start=\\\"3609\\\" data-end=\\\"3619\\\">6 days<\\/strong> of termination for fired employees.<\\/p>\\n<hr data-start=\\\"3657\\\" data-end=\\\"3660\\\">\\n<h2 data-start=\\\"3662\\\" data-end=\\\"3724\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"3665\\\" data-end=\\\"3724\\\">What Are Your Legal Rights Under Texas and Federal Law?<\\/strong><\\/h2>\\n<p data-start=\\\"3726\\\" data-end=\\\"3755\\\">Your rights are protected by:<\\/p>\\n<ul data-start=\\\"3757\\\" data-end=\\\"4007\\\">\\n<li data-start=\\\"3757\\\" data-end=\\\"3814\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"3759\\\" data-end=\\\"3814\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"3759\\\" data-end=\\\"3798\\\">The Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA)<\\/strong> \\u2013 Federal law<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"3815\\\" data-end=\\\"3874\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"3817\\\" data-end=\\\"3874\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"3817\\\" data-end=\\\"3837\\\">Texas Payday Law<\\/strong> \\u2013 State law on timely wage payment<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"3875\\\" data-end=\\\"3937\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"3877\\\" data-end=\\\"3937\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"3877\\\" data-end=\\\"3906\\\">Department of Labor (DOL)<\\/strong> \\u2013 Federal enforcement agency<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"3938\\\" data-end=\\\"4007\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"3940\\\" data-end=\\\"4007\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"3940\\\" data-end=\\\"3976\\\">Texas Workforce Commission (TWC)<\\/strong> \\u2013 State agency for wage claims<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p data-start=\\\"4009\\\" data-end=\\\"4050\\\">Employers who violate these laws may owe:<\\/p>\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4052\\\" data-end=\\\"4168\\\">\\n<li data-start=\\\"4052\\\" data-end=\\\"4068\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4054\\\" data-end=\\\"4068\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"4054\\\" data-end=\\\"4066\\\">Back pay<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4069\\\" data-end=\\\"4120\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4071\\\" data-end=\\\"4120\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"4071\\\" data-end=\\\"4093\\\">Liquidated damages<\\/strong> (double the amount owed)<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4121\\\" data-end=\\\"4139\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4123\\\" data-end=\\\"4139\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"4123\\\" data-end=\\\"4137\\\">Legal fees<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4140\\\" data-end=\\\"4168\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4142\\\" data-end=\\\"4168\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"4142\\\" data-end=\\\"4168\\\">Interest and penalties<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<hr data-start=\\\"4170\\\" data-end=\\\"4173\\\">\\n<h2 data-start=\\\"4175\\\" data-end=\\\"4224\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"4178\\\" data-end=\\\"4224\\\">Who Is Protected Under Wage and Hour Laws?<\\/strong><\\/h2>\\n<p data-start=\\\"4226\\\" data-end=\\\"4270\\\">Nearly all employees are covered, including:<\\/p>\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4272\\\" data-end=\\\"4428\\\">\\n<li data-start=\\\"4272\\\" data-end=\\\"4290\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4274\\\" data-end=\\\"4290\\\">Hourly workers<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4291\\\" data-end=\\\"4324\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4293\\\" data-end=\\\"4324\\\">Salaried non-exempt employees<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4325\\\" data-end=\\\"4345\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4327\\\" data-end=\\\"4345\\\">Tipped employees<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4346\\\" data-end=\\\"4373\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4348\\\" data-end=\\\"4373\\\">Interns (in some cases)<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4374\\\" data-end=\\\"4428\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4376\\\" data-end=\\\"4428\\\">Freelancers misclassified as independent contractors<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p data-start=\\\"4430\\\" data-end=\\\"4555\\\">However, some <strong data-start=\\\"4444\\\" data-end=\\\"4464\\\">exempt employees<\\/strong>\\u2014like executives, professionals, and some outside salespeople\\u2014may not qualify for overtime.<\\/p>\\n<p data-start=\\\"4557\\\" data-end=\\\"4683\\\">A <strong data-start=\\\"4559\\\" data-end=\\\"4583\\\">wage and hour lawyer<\\/strong> at <strong data-start=\\\"4587\\\" data-end=\\\"4605\\\">The Lange Firm<\\/strong> can review your job duties to determine whether you were properly classified.<\\/p>\\n<hr data-start=\\\"4685\\\" data-end=\\\"4688\\\">\\n<h2 data-start=\\\"4690\\\" data-end=\\\"4744\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"4693\\\" data-end=\\\"4744\\\">Signs You Should Contact a Wage and Hour Lawyer<\\/strong><\\/h2>\\n<p data-start=\\\"4746\\\" data-end=\\\"4776\\\">You should seek legal help if:<\\/p>\\n<ul data-start=\\\"4778\\\" data-end=\\\"5197\\\">\\n<li data-start=\\\"4778\\\" data-end=\\\"4841\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4780\\\" data-end=\\\"4841\\\">You regularly work over 40 hours and don\\u2019t receive overtime<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4842\\\" data-end=\\\"4885\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4844\\\" data-end=\\\"4885\\\">You\\u2019re not paid minimum wage after tips<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4886\\\" data-end=\\\"4944\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4888\\\" data-end=\\\"4944\\\">Your employer asks you to \\u201cclock out and keep working\\u201d<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4945\\\" data-end=\\\"4994\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4947\\\" data-end=\\\"4994\\\">Your paycheck contains unexplained deductions<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"4995\\\" data-end=\\\"5041\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"4997\\\" data-end=\\\"5041\\\">You haven\\u2019t been paid for all hours worked<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5042\\\" data-end=\\\"5084\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5044\\\" data-end=\\\"5084\\\">You didn\\u2019t receive your final paycheck<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5085\\\" data-end=\\\"5145\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5087\\\" data-end=\\\"5145\\\">You\\u2019re asked to sign away your rights or confidentiality<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5146\\\" data-end=\\\"5197\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5148\\\" data-end=\\\"5197\\\">You\\u2019re fired after asking about pay discrepancies<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p data-start=\\\"5199\\\" data-end=\\\"5293\\\">Don\\u2019t wait\\u2014<strong data-start=\\\"5210\\\" data-end=\\\"5254\\\">Texas wage claims have short time limits<\\/strong>, and the clock may already be ticking.<\\/p>\\n<hr data-start=\\\"5295\\\" data-end=\\\"5298\\\">\\n<h2 data-start=\\\"5300\\\" data-end=\\\"5345\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"5303\\\" data-end=\\\"5345\\\">How to Prove a Wage and Hour Violation<\\/strong><\\/h2>\\n<p data-start=\\\"5347\\\" data-end=\\\"5371\\\">Evidence is key. Gather:<\\/p>\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5373\\\" data-end=\\\"5571\\\">\\n<li data-start=\\\"5373\\\" data-end=\\\"5403\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5375\\\" data-end=\\\"5403\\\">Timecards or punch records<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5404\\\" data-end=\\\"5436\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5406\\\" data-end=\\\"5436\\\">Paystubs and wage statements<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5437\\\" data-end=\\\"5472\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5439\\\" data-end=\\\"5472\\\">Work schedules or text messages<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5473\\\" data-end=\\\"5497\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5475\\\" data-end=\\\"5497\\\">Emails from managers<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5498\\\" data-end=\\\"5535\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5500\\\" data-end=\\\"5535\\\">Screenshots from clock-in systems<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5536\\\" data-end=\\\"5571\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5538\\\" data-end=\\\"5571\\\">Witness statements from coworkers<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p data-start=\\\"5573\\\" data-end=\\\"5715\\\">Even if you don\\u2019t have perfect records, <strong data-start=\\\"5613\\\" data-end=\\\"5631\\\">The Lange Firm<\\/strong> can help reconstruct your case and use subpoena power to demand employer documents.<\\/p>\\n<hr data-start=\\\"5717\\\" data-end=\\\"5720\\\">\\n<h2 data-start=\\\"5722\\\" data-end=\\\"5752\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"5725\\\" data-end=\\\"5752\\\">Damages You May Recover<\\/strong><\\/h2>\\n<p data-start=\\\"5754\\\" data-end=\\\"5805\\\">Employees who win wage and hour claims may recover:<\\/p>\\n<ul data-start=\\\"5807\\\" data-end=\\\"5994\\\">\\n<li data-start=\\\"5807\\\" data-end=\\\"5827\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5809\\\" data-end=\\\"5827\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"5809\\\" data-end=\\\"5825\\\">Unpaid wages<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5828\\\" data-end=\\\"5848\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5830\\\" data-end=\\\"5848\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"5830\\\" data-end=\\\"5846\\\">Overtime pay<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5849\\\" data-end=\\\"5901\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5851\\\" data-end=\\\"5901\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"5851\\\" data-end=\\\"5873\\\">Liquidated damages<\\/strong> (up to 2x the wages owed)<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5902\\\" data-end=\\\"5925\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5904\\\" data-end=\\\"5925\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"5904\\\" data-end=\\\"5923\\\">Attorney\\u2019s fees<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5926\\\" data-end=\\\"5956\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5928\\\" data-end=\\\"5956\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"5928\\\" data-end=\\\"5954\\\">Interest and penalties<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"5957\\\" data-end=\\\"5994\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"5959\\\" data-end=\\\"5994\\\">In rare cases, <strong data-start=\\\"5974\\\" data-end=\\\"5994\\\">punitive damages<\\/strong><\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p data-start=\\\"5996\\\" data-end=\\\"6085\\\">In class or collective actions, entire groups of employees may recover large settlements.<\\/p>\\n<hr data-start=\\\"6087\\\" data-end=\\\"6090\\\">\\n<h2 data-start=\\\"6092\\\" data-end=\\\"6142\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"6095\\\" data-end=\\\"6142\\\">What to Expect When You Hire The Lange Firm<\\/strong><\\/h2>\\n<p data-start=\\\"6144\\\" data-end=\\\"6174\\\">Here\\u2019s what we do for clients:<\\/p>\\n<ol data-start=\\\"6176\\\" data-end=\\\"6443\\\">\\n<li data-start=\\\"6176\\\" data-end=\\\"6222\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"6179\\\" data-end=\\\"6222\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"6179\\\" data-end=\\\"6200\\\">Initial consultation<\\/strong> to assess your case<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"6223\\\" data-end=\\\"6278\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"6226\\\" data-end=\\\"6278\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"6226\\\" data-end=\\\"6244\\\">Legal analysis<\\/strong> of wage and hour law violations<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"6279\\\" data-end=\\\"6336\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"6282\\\" data-end=\\\"6336\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"6282\\\" data-end=\\\"6308\\\">Settlement negotiation<\\/strong> or employer demand letter<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"6337\\\" data-end=\\\"6379\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"6340\\\" data-end=\\\"6379\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"6340\\\" data-end=\\\"6366\\\">Filing with DOL or TWC<\\/strong>, if needed<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<li data-start=\\\"6380\\\" data-end=\\\"6443\\\">\\n<p data-start=\\\"6383\\\" data-end=\\\"6443\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"6383\\\" data-end=\\\"6420\\\">Lawsuit in state or federal court<\\/strong>, if employer won\\u2019t pay<\\/p>\\n<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n<p data-start=\\\"6445\\\" data-end=\\\"6554\\\">We handle many cases on a <strong data-start=\\\"6471\\\" data-end=\\\"6496\\\">contingency fee basis<\\/strong>\\u2014meaning no legal fees unless we win or settle your claim.<\\/p>\\n<hr data-start=\\\"6556\\\" data-end=\\\"6559\\\">\\n<h2 data-start=\\\"6561\\\" data-end=\\\"6604\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"6564\\\" data-end=\\\"6604\\\">Texas Wage and Hour Laws at a Glance<\\/strong><\\/h2>\\n<div class=\\\"_tableContainer_16hzy_1\\\">\\n<div class=\\\"_tableWrapper_16hzy_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\\\" tabindex=\\\"-1\\\">\\n<table class=\\\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\\\" data-start=\\\"6606\\\" data-end=\\\"7236\\\">\\n<thead data-start=\\\"6606\\\" data-end=\\\"6683\\\">\\n<tr data-start=\\\"6606\\\" data-end=\\\"6683\\\">\\n<th data-start=\\\"6606\\\" data-end=\\\"6636\\\" data-col-size=\\\"sm\\\"><strong data-start=\\\"6608\\\" data-end=\\\"6620\\\">Category<\\/strong><\\/th>\\n<th data-start=\\\"6636\\\" data-end=\\\"6683\\\" d